{"question": "What elements must be included in the continuous monitoring strategy and program?", "framework_version": "rev4", "answer_text": "The continuous monitoring strategy and program must include the following elements, which depend on organization-defined parameters:

1. Establishment of organization-defined metrics/elements to be monitored (ca-7_prm_1);
2. Establishment of organization-defined frequencies for monitoring (ca-7_prm_2) and organization-defined frequencies for assessments supporting such monitoring (ca-7_prm_3);
3. Ongoing security control assessments in accordance with the organizational continuous monitoring strategy;
4. Ongoing security status monitoring of organization-defined metrics in accordance with the organizational continuous monitoring strategy;
5. Correlation and analysis of security-related information generated by assessments and monitoring;
6. Response actions to address results of the analysis of security-related information; and
7. Reporting the security status of the organization and the information system to organization-defined personnel/roles (ca-7_prm_4) at organization-defined frequencies (ca-7_prm_5).", "answer_text_with_citations": "The continuous monitoring strategy and program must include the following elements, which depend on organization-defined parameters:

1. Establishment of organization-defined metrics/elements to be monitored (ca-7_prm_1);
2. Establishment of organization-defined frequencies for monitoring (ca-7_prm_2) and organization-defined frequencies for assessments supporting such monitoring (ca-7_prm_3);
3. Ongoing security control assessments in accordance with the organizational continuous monitoring strategy;
4. Ongoing security status monitoring of organization-defined metrics in accordance with the organizational continuous monitoring strategy;
5. Correlation and analysis of security-related information generated by assessments and monitoring;
6. Response actions to address results of the analysis of security-related information; and
7. Reporting the security status of the organization and the information system to organization-defined personnel/roles (ca-7_prm_4) at organization-defined frequencies (ca-7_prm_5).

