{"question": "What does MP-6 require for sanitizing media prior to disposal or release?", "framework_version": "rev4", "answer_text": "MP-6 requires the organization to sanitize the organization-defined media prior to disposal, release out of organizational control, or release for reuse using organization-defined sanitization techniques and procedures in accordance with applicable federal and organizational standards and policies. Additionally, the organization must employ sanitization mechanisms with a strength and integrity commensurate with the security category or classification of the information.", "answer_text_with_citations": "MP-6 requires the organization to sanitize the organization-defined media prior to disposal, release out of organizational control, or release for reuse using organization-defined sanitization techniques and procedures in accordance with applicable federal and organizational standards and policies. Additionally, the organization must employ sanitization mechanisms with a strength and integrity commensurate with the security category or classification of the information.

