{"question": "What does SI-2 require for identifying, reporting, and correcting system flaws?", "framework_version": "rev4", "answer_text": "According to SI-2, the organization is required to identify, report, and correct information system flaws; test software and firmware updates related to flaw remediation for effectiveness and potential side effects before installation; install security-relevant software and firmware updates within an organization-defined time period of the release of the updates; and incorporate flaw remediation into the organizational configuration management process.", "answer_text_with_citations": "According to SI-2, the organization is required to identify, report, and correct information system flaws; test software and firmware updates related to flaw remediation for effectiveness and potential side effects before installation; install security-relevant software and firmware updates within an organization-defined time period of the release of the updates; and incorporate flaw remediation into the organizational configuration management process.

